en:
I see.
I thought as much.
The legend of this cherry tree isn't as simple as you all think.{p}

Of course you are.
I think anyone would be interested.
Anyone who answers that they aren't interested is a liar.{p}

Back then, high school students were all still innocent.
They were the kind who were embarrassed even to hold hands.
A kiss took tremendous resolve.{p}

It was said that if anyone else saw two lovers at the moment of their kiss, the pair would meet a tragic end.
That's why hardly any couples managed to carry out the legend.
Tell someone, and they'd come to watch for fun; tell no one, and there was still the chance of being seen by accident.{p}

When the cherry tree appeared as a silhouette in the moonlight, the two of them held their breath at its sheer beauty.
It was a truly dreamlike scene.
But at that moment, they also saw something they should never have seen.{p}

"An admirable attitude. Then I shall let you take responsibility. Come to me."
"To you...?"
"I am the spirit of the cherry tree. Now, come to me."{p}

The two of them did as the cherry tree spirit asked.
And they kissed.
At that moment...{p}

...I'm sorry, {a}{f:|}.
It must feel as if I've tricked you.
But it can't be helped.{p}

...Well, that's the end of my story.
Now then, let's go back to the newspaper club room.
The seven wonders aren't over yet, after all...{p}

You're awfully down-to-earth, aren't you?
But no such rumor is actually going around, so of course you can't really answer when I ask you like this.
That's how little anyone knows about it.{p}

"Let's make it early tomorrow morning. Tomorrow's Sunday, after all."
Having said only that, Orihara hung her head.
Seeing her like that, Hirooka felt his chest fill with warmth.{p}

And so, early the next morning, the two of them met at the school gate.
Not a word passed between them.
Their hearts were as one, so they had no need for words.{p}

Then they came beneath the cherry tree and faced each other.
Hirooka placed his hands on Orihara's shoulders.
Trembling slightly, Orihara closed her eyes.{p}

And just as their lips touched...
"Ah!"
They heard a small cry.{p}

The two of them gasped and turned toward the voice.
And there stood a girl, a student.
She had happened to pass by and had seen Hirooka and Orihara's ritual.{p}

"...I'll leave it up to you."
That was all Orihara could manage to say.
So Hirooka said...{p}

......The next day, I hear there was a huge uproar.
Well, of course there was.
Four people dead in a single night.{p}

"{f:Waaaaugh|Eeeeek}!"
{f:I|I} leapt back without thinking.
I landed on my backside.{p}

This is a true story.
And that's the end of my story.
Now, shall we go back to the club room?{p}

Unable to bear how terrifying his face looked right in front of her, she squeezed her eyes shut.
Just then.
"Aaaah!"{p}

That is the true story behind this cherry tree.
Ever since then, they say, this cherry tree has craved living blood.
Every year, one sacrifice is offered up to it.{p}

Heh heh heh, don't come crying to me if you regret it later.
Well, for now, let me compose myself and go on with my story.
I'll tell you how I know this story...{p}

Don't be scared!
I'm not thinking of making you a sacrifice or anything...
After all, I've already offered up my third sacrifice.{p}

Heh heh heh.
What's the matter with you?
Are you scared already?{p}
